# Code owners.
#
# One owner, deliberately. This is a single-author repository, and a
# `CODEOWNERS` file listing eight people for a 199-line teaching artifact would be
# a way of appearing well-governed.
#
# The two entries that are not "everything" are the two places where a wrong
# change is *silently* wrong rather than loudly wrong, which is the criterion
# that decides whether a path needs a more careful review:
#
#   reference/  byte-pinned; every number in the repository is a claim about
#               these exact bytes
#   traces/     the evidence behind every number; a drift here invalidates prose
#               that nothing would otherwise flag as stale

*                       @DenimPatel

# The reference and its annotated fork. CI checks the sha256 of microgpt.py, so
# a change here must also update tools/provenance.py, bump PIN_EPOCH, and
# regenerate the traces and the benchmarks. See docs/TRACE-FORMAT.md.
reference/             @DenimPatel

# Recorded runs. Regenerate rather than hand-edit, and review the prose that
# quotes the numbers.
traces/                @DenimPatel

# The C backward pass. docs/KNOWN-ISSUES.md issue 1: the directional-derivative
# ratio is locked at -0.12 +/- 0.20, so any change to implementations/c/*.c
# trips that test on purpose.
implementations/c/      @DenimPatel
